WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:03.600
When it comes to popular movies, everyone's
got theories.

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:08.200
There's just something so gratifying about
diving deep into the finest details of a film

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.559
and coming up with a plausible connection
others haven't yet seen.

00:00:11.559 --> 00:00:15.429
Even more exhilarating are those times when
those theories are eventually confirmed by

00:00:15.429 --> 00:00:17.240
the people involved in a project.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:21.420
In the case of these cinematic conjectures,
fans were able to figure out certain connections

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.850
long before they were ultimately confirmed
by those in the know.

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:28.180
And as always … beware the spoilers!

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:29.180
The Logan prophecy

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:34.789
2013's The Wolverine might've seemed like
just another installment of Logan's long history

00:00:34.789 --> 00:00:36.140
on the big screen.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:41.030
But as one fan on Twitter noticed, the film's
clairvoyant character Yukio predicted Logan's

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:42.030
ultimate fate.

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:43.829
"I saw you die.

00:00:43.829 --> 00:00:52.149
I see you on your back, there's blood everywhere,
and you're holding your own heart in your

00:00:52.149 --> 00:00:53.149
hand."

00:00:53.149 --> 00:00:56.530
At the end of Logan, of course, that's almost
exactly what happened.

00:00:56.530 --> 00:01:00.999
A few years later, the character died in the
movie Logan, while lying on his back and covered

00:01:00.999 --> 00:01:03.059
in blood, as was foretold.

00:01:03.059 --> 00:01:07.910
And while he wasn't holding his literal heart
in his hand, he was clasping the hand of his

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:11.770
cloned "daughter" Laura a.k.a. X-23.

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:14.190
The connection was not a coincidence.

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:17.970
Director James Mangold later praised the person
who first drew the connection between the

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:21.070
scenes and thus confirmed it was his intention
all along.

00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:23.800
"I would agree with your observations.

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:25.440
Cars takeover

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:30.600
While most people wouldn't think too deeply
about a Pixar movie starring talking automobiles,

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:35.780
some adults — and maybe even some kids — left
screenings of Cars with a disturbing thought:

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:37.300
where are the humans?

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:41.050
After all, it's not like humans never inhabited
the world of Cars.

00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:45.440
Proof of human existence is littered throughout
the entire movie, from door handles to road

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:46.700
signs and more.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:49.380
So, what exactly happened to us?

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:53.340
One fan theory proposed that the cars themselves
eliminated humans.

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:56.340
And as it turns out, that's actually what
happened.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:02:00.680
According to Jay Ward, the Creative Director
of the Cars universe, the anthropomorphic

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:02.880
autos simply didn't need the dead weight.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:07.690
He said, "Imagine in the near-future when
the cars keep getting smarter and smarter

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:11.300
and after one day they just go, 'Why do we
need human beings anymore?

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:13.290
They're just slowing us down.

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:15.380
It's just extra weight, let's get rid of them.'

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:18.990
But the car takes on the personality of the
last person who drove it…

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:19.990
There you go."

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:24.270
Who knew a global robot domination story could
be so kid-friendly?

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:26.640
The Frozen-Tarzan connection

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:31.580
When Frozen co-directors Jennifer Lee and
Chris Buck took to Reddit for an Ask Us Anything,

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:36.069
they blew everyone's minds when they revealed
that, despite the film 's opening montage,

00:02:36.069 --> 00:02:39.440
Anna and Elsa's parents didn't actually die
at sea.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:45.100
Instead, Buck stated the protagonists' parents
"got washed up on a shore in a jungle island.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:47.350
The queen gave birth to a baby boy.

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:48.690
They build a treehouse.

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:50.730
They get eaten by a leopard…"

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:54.970
That sounded a lot like what some fans had
theorized about the backstory of the orphaned

00:02:54.970 --> 00:03:00.460
Tarzan and how he might actually be the long
lost brother of Anna and Elsa.

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:04.290
Buck later confirmed to MTV that fans were
right on the money with their origin theory

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:07.720
— at least when it comes to how the story
plays out in his head.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:11.500
He explained: "Of course Anna and Elsa's parents
didn't die.'

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:15.540
Yes, there was a shipwreck, but they were
at sea a little bit longer than we think they

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:20.780
were because the mother was pregnant, and
she gave birth on the boat, to a little boy.

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:26.720
They get shipwrecked, and somehow they really
washed way far away from the Scandinavian

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:28.800
waters, and they end up in the jungle.

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:33.590
They end up building a treehouse and a leopard
kills them, so their baby boy is raised by

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:34.680
gorillas.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:38.680
So in my little head, Anna and Elsa's brother
is Tarzan."

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:42.910
It's too bad Tarzan didn't inherit his sister's
gift for whipping up ice sculptures to help

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:44.780
his jungle pals beat the heat.

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:49.390
But at least the director didn't come out
and tell fans to let it go and stick to the

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:50.620
elephant's wild theory.

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:55.700
"You know I've been thinking lately that maybe
Tarzan could be some subspecies of elephant."

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.320
The Genie peddler

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:03.690
Another Disney animation theory that's gotten
the official thumbs up is that the Genie from

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:08.849
Aladdin appeared in the film long before the
street rat ever rubbed that magic lamp.

00:04:08.849 --> 00:04:12.910
Fans noticed the peculiar behaviors of the
peddler who introduced the movie and figured

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:17.739
out that he and the Genie were the same guy,
now free from the confines of the lamp.

00:04:17.739 --> 00:04:20.150
"Do not be fooled by its commonplace appearance.

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:25.450
Like so many things, it's not what's outside,
but what's inside that counts."

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:29.970
Director Ron Clements later admitted the theory
was true and said, "That was the whole intention,

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:30.970
originally."

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:34.840
We even had that at the end of the movie,
where he would reveal himself to be the Genie

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:38.010
… and of course Robin [Williams] did the
voice of the peddler.

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:41.880
Just through story changes and some editing,
we lost the reveal at the end.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.450
So, that's an urban legend that actually is
true."

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.450
"Look at me from the side.

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:46.910
Do I look different to you?"

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:49.550
Spider-Man's true MCU debut

00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:53.280
There's been a long-running theory amongst
fans of the Marvel Cinematic Universe that

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:57.280
Peter Parker showed up even earlier than Captain
America: Civil War.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:01.389
As the story goes, the little kid who dressed
like Iron Man and mean mugged a robot at the

00:05:01.389 --> 00:05:05.300
Stark Expo in Iron Man 2 is actually a young
Peter Parker.

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:10.010
Iron Man 2 was released in 2010, after all,
and everyone's favorite neighborhood web slinger

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:13.750
was still in his mid-teens in 2017's Spider-Man:
Homecoming.

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:18.860
Furthermore, the aforementioned Stark Expo
takes place in Parker's hometown of Queens.

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:23.060
Tom Holland himself has now confirmed this
idea as MCU official.

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:24.140
"Badass."

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:29.130
The actor who plays Spidey told Huffington
Post, "It is Peter Parker … I can confirm

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:30.310
that as of today.

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:34.790
I literally had a conversation with Kevin
Feige only 20 minutes ago.

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:37.840
Maybe I've just done a big, old spoiler, but
it's out there now.

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:38.840
It's cool.

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:41.540
I like the idea that Peter Parker has been
in the universe since the beginning."

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:44.740
"Hi guys!

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:47.620
Wait a minute, you guys aren't the real Avengers.

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:48.840
I can tell.

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:49.840
Hulk gives it away."

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:52.110
Stan Lee is a Watcher

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:56.940
Anyone who regularly watches Marvel movies
is undoubtedly accustomed to the regular Stan

00:05:56.940 --> 00:05:57.940
Lee cameos.

00:05:57.940 --> 00:06:02.080
The comic book legend has made an appearance
in almost every Marvel movie ever made.

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:03.910
"Look at Mr. Smiles over here.

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:04.910
Where's your wife old man?"

00:06:04.910 --> 00:06:08.680
Lee's cameos have always been written off
as merely nods to Marvel's main man, but some

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:14.250
fans suspected he might be one of The Watchers
— a race of aliens who observe and compile

00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:19.310
information on everything the universe has
to offer, while refraining from interference.

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:21.300
Lee himself denied the theory at first.

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:29.960
Though I'll admit I'm a wonderful human being."

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:34.220
But Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2 director
James Gunn decided to have a little fun and

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:35.610
make the theory legit.

00:06:35.610 --> 00:06:41.270
In the 2017 film, Gunn added a post-credit
scene in which Lee regales The Watchers with

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:42.700
stories of his adventures.

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:56.420
The director then told Radio Times, "There's
a lot of cool stuff that the fans come up

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:57.419
with.

00:06:57.419 --> 00:06:58.740
A lot of stuff I don't agree with...

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:03.729
But I find the idea that Stan Lee is a Watcher,
or that he works for the Watchers, is just

00:07:03.729 --> 00:07:05.289
a fun little nod to the fans."

00:07:05.289 --> 00:07:10.770
Thanks to those fan suggestions, Stan Lee's
stellar role in the MCU is now official.

00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:17.400
"Y'know, I guess one person can make a difference.

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:18.140
Nuff said."

00:07:20.850 --> 00:07:21.940
Thanks for watching!

00:07:21.949 --> 00:07:24.450
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:26.680
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

